  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>
        <figure class="unnumbered">
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_15_09_01.jpg" />
          </media>
        
      </para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 5, use the following scenario to graph an inequality from a table:</para>
      <para>
        <quote>Andre is making trail mix with dried fruit and mixed nuts. Dried fruit costs $3 per
        pound and mixed nuts cost $6 per pound. He wants to spend no more than $54 on the trail mix.
        The inequality \(y \leq −2x + 18\) represents the number of pounds of dried fruit, \(y\), he
        can buy for \(x\) pounds of nuts.</quote>
      </para>
      <!--Q#1-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>The related equation \(y = -2x + 18\) represents the boundary line of the
            inequality. Complete the table of values to find points on the boundary line of the
            inequality.</para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable unnumbered">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <thead>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>0</entry>
                  <entry />
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry />
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry />
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                  <entry />
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>

          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable unnumbered">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <thead>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>0</entry>
                  <entry>18</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>14</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>10</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
